### Pointing the DUT's 802.1X at the testbox instead of at its own local server

```
awplus#configure terminal
awplus(config)#radius-server host 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 key cknotify2026
awplus(config)#aaa group server radius ckbox
awplus(config-sg)#server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812
awplus(config-sg)#exit
awplus(config)#aaa authentication dot1x default group ckbox
awplus(config)#exit
```

**A named group was used on purpose.** `aaa authentication dot1x default group radius` means
*all* configured RADIUS servers, which would still have included the local `127.0.0.1` entry the
rest of the group runs on. `aaa group server radius ckbox` with one member points **only** this
case's 802.1X at the testbox, leaves the local server and its NAS entry untouched for cases 1–3
and for group B, and is removed in one line at teardown.

🔴 **The LOGIN method list was not touched.** Only `aaa authentication dot1x` was changed.
`platforms/x960.md` §7E.1 records that pointing a *login* list at RADIUS has already cost a
console on this exact unit.

Verified before any leg: `show radius` listed both `127.0.0.1` (port 1812) and `10.38.22.33`
(port 11812).

